.mbta__dotcomchrome__call-us-container {
  background: #e2ecf9;
  border-radius: 40px 0 0;
  flex-basis: 30%;
  margin-bottom: -50px;
  padding-bottom: 0;
  padding-top: 40px;
}
.mbta__dotcomchrome__call-us-container .mbta__dotcomchrome__m-footer__links {
  margin-bottom: 0;
  scroll-margin-top: 40vh;
  /*
  When navigating to the customer_support page+anchor from a different page in mobile view,
  the browser would scroll too far down and put the anchor above the top of the screen.  
  Research seems to indicate this is a side effect of scrolling down a fixed header in 
  order to see and click the link.  This scrolling seems to be added to the anchor scroll 
  when the new page loads.  A CSS rule to add some margin between the top of the screen 
  and the anchor seems to work well enough in all circumstances.
  */
}
